From 49bb1c2cddf165c9e2c4f59dd10b857b5e918ba2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:59:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Replace portrait with interactive 3D planet hero
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a teal procedural planet (Uranus-inspired) built with Three.js and
React Three Fiber in place of the static portrait/video on the home page.

- PlanetHero.tsx: custom GLSL shader with animated horizontal banding and
  Fresnel rim glow; additive atmosphere sphere; Stars background from drei;
  OrbitControls with auto-rotate and damping (stops on prefers-reduced-motion)
- Six section points (About, Experience, Contact on the front hemisphere;
  Projects, Education, Skills hidden behind the globe) — each a pulsing dot
  with a pill label that fades in/out via dot-product occlusion check every
  frame, no React re-renders; clicking any point navigates to that section
- PlanetHeroLoader.tsx: thin "use client" wrapper so the ssr:false dynamic
  import is legal from the server-side app/page.tsx
- Hero.tsx: removes mouse-parallax from the portrait slot (would conflict
  with OrbitControls pointer handling)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VcEoceqxMDTGdsAMXZxeDw
